-- input.md --
A fence whose info string is `math` is display math, as on GitHub:

```math
\sqrt{x^2 + 1}
```

One the converter rejects is shown as the code block it would be without math:

```math
\begin{matrix}
a & b
```

Other fences are code:

```Math
x^2
```

```latex
x^2
```
-- output.html --
<p>A fence whose info string is <code>math</code> is display math, as on GitHub:</p>
<math class="math-displaystyle" display="block" displaystyle="true" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{x^2 + 1}
</annotation></semantics></math>
<p>One the converter rejects is shown as the code block it would be without math:</p>
<pre><code class="language-math">\begin{matrix}
a &amp; b
</code></pre>
<p>Other fences are code:</p>
<pre><code class="language-Math">x^2
</code></pre>
<pre><code class="language-latex">x^2
</code></pre>
